# When setting these on Vercel from a shell, pipe with `printf`, not `echo`:
#
#   printf 'agent_xxx' | vercel env add NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID production
#
# `echo` appends a newline, which Vercel stores as part of the value and Next
# inlines verbatim into the client bundle. Both Production values currently
# carry one. The code trims at the read sites, so it is harmless — but a clean
# value is one less thing depending on that.

# ElevenLabs
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID=

# Firecrawl. Server-only: read by /api/firecrawl-search, never exposed to the client.
#
# The agent's `firecrawl_search` is an ElevenLabs *client* tool, not a server
# webhook: the SDK runs it in the browser, which fetches /api/firecrawl-search
# same-origin (see src/app/debate/page.tsx). ElevenLabs' servers never call us.
# That is why the same-origin check in the route can reject origin-less requests
# without breaking a debate -- do not relax it on the assumption that ElevenLabs
# calls in from outside.
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
